{"id": "q0435", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 4147165912, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "Who are the top NFL Quarterbacks?", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0435.wav", "input_sha256": "76e25f78573b3827ab9e1d37488f278a1702e8964fd422175326798024b26a18", "input_samples": 31600, "input_s": 1.975, "n_real_chunks": 2, "score": 0.8186, "act": 0.9983, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "As of the start of the 2026 NFL season, the usual “top QB” tier is: Josh Allen — Buffalo Bills , Patrick Mahomes — Kansas City Chiefs , Joe Burrow — Cincinnati Bengals , Lamar Jackson — Baltimore Ravens , Matthew Stafford — Los Angeles Rams That top group is supported by recent rankings: PFF has Allen, Burrow, Lamar, Mahomes in its top tier, while AP writers voted Josh Allen the top QB, followed by Mahomes, Stafford, Lamar, and Burrow. (pff.com) Other quarterbacks commonly in the next tier include Justin Herbert, Jalen Hurts, C.J. Stroud, Dak Prescott, Jared Goff, and Brock Purdy.", "expert_answer": "As of the start of the **2026 NFL season**, the usual “top QB” tier is:\n\n1. **Josh Allen — Buffalo Bills**\n2. **Patrick Mahomes — Kansas City Chiefs**\n3. **Joe Burrow — Cincinnati Bengals**\n4. **Lamar Jackson — Baltimore Ravens**\n5. **Matthew Stafford — Los Angeles Rams**\n\nThat top group is supported by recent rankings: PFF has **Allen, Burrow, Lamar, Mahomes** in its top tier, while AP writers voted **Josh Allen** the top QB, followed by **Mahomes, Stafford, Lamar, and Burrow**. ([pff.com](https://www.pff.com/news/nfl-player-rankings?utm_source=openai))\n\nOther quarterbacks commonly in the next tier include **Justin Herbert, Jalen Hurts, C.J. Stroud, Dak Prescott, Jared Goff, and Brock Purdy**.", "transcript": "Who are the top NFL quarterbacks?\n", "asr_s": 0.77, "expert_s": 5.9, "expert_input_samples": 31600, "expert_input_s": 1.975, "expert_input_sha256": "76e25f78573b3827ab9e1d37488f278a1702e8964fd422175326798024b26a18", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 5.151, "relay_synth_ms": 24578, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 576, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 576, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0435_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "f18a444ae0aeff75eb36a084241fdb7d50e2ade670690d2267c8127c3ef93c1c", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 41.04}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0435_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "69bb2f0b308b0daa82bee2c972a66b1d0bd6efa50243216a62604dc04f37b83a", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0435_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "a2e918afd68ae51950986ca19eda5b828dbcb84963907285b08436229a9bdfe0", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.078, 1.14, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 1.975, 2.051, 2.111, 1, 0, 0], [2, 0, 2.975, 3.056, 3.117, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.975, 4.052, 4.921, 0, 24000, 0], [4, 0, 4.975, 5.626, 6.438, 0, 30720, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 1.975, "last_real_feed_done": 2.051, "onset": 4.921, "gate_read_done": 4.921, "fire": 4.921, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.921, "stall_note": 4.922, "stall_first_pcm": 5.551, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 6.438, "expert_req": 4.922, "expert_resp": 11.589, "relay_synth_start": 11.589, "relay_first_pcm": 12.457, "relay_synth_end": 36.168, "first_any_pcm": 4.921, "first_answer_pcm": 12.457, "session_end": 36.594}, "ttfa_answer_s": 10.482, "ttfa_any_s": 2.946}
{"id": "q0459", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2833011061, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "What are some basic spirits you should have at your bar", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0459.wav", "input_sha256": "b29397119c0a30b55bf41a0cf43e057efabfde6654c1c5de5231e6048ba54b24", "input_samples": 52400, "input_s": 3.275, "n_real_chunks": 4, "score": 0.7109, "act": 0.9989, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Some basic spirits to keep in a home bar are: Vodka – neutral base for many cocktails , Gin – essential for martinis, gin & tonics, negronis , Rum – at least a white rum; dark or aged rum is useful too , Tequila – preferably 100% agave blanco or reposado , Whiskey – bourbon or rye for classics like Old Fashioneds and Manhattans , Scotch – optional, but good if you or guests enjoy it neat or in cocktails , Brandy/Cognac – useful for Sidecars and other classic drinks If you’re starting small, the core five are vodka, gin, rum, tequila, and whiskey.", "expert_answer": "Some basic spirits to keep in a home bar are:\n\n- **Vodka** – neutral base for many cocktails  \n- **Gin** – essential for martinis, gin & tonics, negronis  \n- **Rum** – at least a white rum; dark or aged rum is useful too  \n- **Tequila** – preferably 100% agave blanco or reposado  \n- **Whiskey** – bourbon or rye for classics like Old Fashioneds and Manhattans  \n- **Scotch** – optional, but good if you or guests enjoy it neat or in cocktails  \n- **Brandy/Cognac** – useful for Sidecars and other classic drinks  \n\nIf you’re starting small, the core five are **vodka, gin, rum, tequila, and whiskey**.", "transcript": "What are some basic spirits you should have at your bar?\n", "asr_s": 0.96, "expert_s": 4.22, "expert_input_samples": 52400, "expert_input_s": 3.275, "expert_input_sha256": "b29397119c0a30b55bf41a0cf43e057efabfde6654c1c5de5231e6048ba54b24", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 0.0, "relay_synth_ms": 23284, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 19, "feed_lag_max_ms": 137, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 141, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0459_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "1ff448729749e18ec5f734fbf927076cb1b8c3cc3b5c778fdeade86b16cea1f5", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 34.44}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0459_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "3edee9b7769c86205079f337b80836854da7b7a626141c8a55c511f4789a66b6", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 20.16}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.077, 1.141, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.076, 2.137, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.077, 3.14, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 3.275, 3.358, 3.745, 0, 0, 0], [4, 0, 4.275, 4.491, 5.138, 0, 24000, 0], [5, 0, 5.275, 5.357, 6.057, 0, 24000, 0], [6, 0, 6.275, 6.353, 7.13, 0, 24000, 0], [7, 0, 7.275, 7.36, 8.28, 0, 24000, 0], [8, 0, 8.275, 8.394, 9.106, 0, 24000, 0], [9, 0, 9.275, 9.359, 10.046, 0, 24000, 0], [10, 0, 10.275, 10.356, 11.125, 0, 24000, 0], [11, 0, 11.275, 11.358, 11.978, 0, 24000, 0], [12, 0, 12.275, 12.349, 13.051, 0, 24000, 0], [13, 0, 13.275, 13.348, 14.044, 0, 24000, 0], [14, 0, 14.275, 14.352, 15.072, 0, 24000, 0], [15, 0, 15.275, 15.351, 16.003, 0, 24000, 0], [16, 0, 16.275, 16.362, 17.109, 0, 24000, 0], [17, 0, 17.275, 17.352, 18.098, 0, 24000, 0], [18, 0, 18.275, 18.361, 19.17, 0, 24000, 0], [19, 0, 19.275, 19.365, 20.194, 0, 24000, 0], [20, 0, 20.275, 20.371, 21.206, 0, 24000, 0], [21, 0, 21.275, 21.374, 22.227, 0, 24000, 0], [22, 0, 22.275, 22.37, 23.098, 0, 27840, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 3.275, "last_real_feed_done": 3.358, "onset": 3.745, "gate_read_done": 3.746, "fire": 3.746, "candidate_first_pcm": null, "s